{
    "background_story": "Tru was a free-spirited musician who spent his life traveling from one train station to another, carrying his guitar and a suitcase full of dreams. He'd hop on a train, play for passengers in exchange for food and shelter, and then get off at the next station, ready to start anew. Tru's music was a reflection of the people and places he encountered along the way. He'd write songs about the bustling streets of New York City, the jazz clubs of New Orleans, and the sunsets of California. As he traveled, Tru became known as the 'Station Songster,' and people would gather at train stations just to hear him play. His music was a constant, a reminder that even in transit, there was beauty to be found. Tru's journey was a never-ending quest to find inspiration in the stations of life.",
